cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use karez or its research in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "karez: standards-shaped database connectivity for Rust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sudheesh
    family-names: PM
repository-code: "https://github.com/cameleering/karez"
url: "https://github.com/cameleering/karez"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - rust
  - database
  - database-driver
  - jdbc
  - odbc
  - adbc
  - apache-arrow
  - postgresql
  - mysql
  - sql-server
  - sqlite
abstract: >-
  karez is a planned Rust database connectivity library: one API and native drivers for
  PostgreSQL, MySQL and MariaDB, SQL Server and SQLite that follows the JDBC, ODBC and ADBC
  standards, decodes results into Apache Arrow columnar chunks, and is exported as ADBC, ODBC
  and JDBC drivers. The repository currently holds the sourced research and the build plan;
  no code has been released and nothing has been measured.
references:
